   "text": {
    "L1": "An angle is the amount of turn between two arms.",
    "L2": "A right angle is a quarter turn, like the corner of a book. Turning the angle does not change its type.",
    "L3": "Use a paper corner to test an angle: smaller is acute, an exact match is right, and wider is obtuse.",
    "L4": "The arms can be long or short. Their length does not change the angle.",
    "L5": "At 3 o'clock, the clock hands make a right angle. At 5 o'clock, the opening is wider.",
    "L6": "It is wider than a right angle but less than a half turn, so the angle at 5 o'clock is obtuse.",
    "L7": "Now choose the type of the angle at 5 o'clock."
   },
